         NodeHeight=544
         NodeComment="If you\'re using ALS, you should populate this function with some logic to set your character\'s InAirRotation and TargetRotation values to the actor\'s current rotation. This is not filled in because it requires you to cast to your own ALS base character class. See the provided documentation for details on what should be put here.\r\n\r\nThis function is called when a wall run or wall jump ends, and it informs ALS what the character\'s rotation should be."
